y disinterested  on the whole I haven't been and I've  been out to the court we gave a victim  impact statement only about four months  ago  in front of the judges this whole  process to me is just so important and  not because of the verdicts  you know in a sense I don't care about  the verdict because  within a couple of weeks of the plane  being shot down it was quite transparent  that the Russians had sent in some  artillery and had shot this plane down  and you know all the denials and the  misinformation that the Russians came  out with well you know you treat that  with a pinch of salt it's a bit like the  other day when they accused the Royal  Navy of blowing up a gas pipeline in  everything the Russians say and do is  our lies and disinformation and nobody  should be in any doubt that everything  we hear from the likes of lavrov to the  United Nations  command should command no respect  so having said that when I heard the  judgment  to my mind whatever whatever the court  had decided was to be the verdict that  would have been fine with me because  I've watched this process and I  understand that whatever whatever they  came out with would be the correct  verdict now they happen to have come out  with a verdict which matches the verdict  I would have liked to have seen so my  response to that  certainly not Elation that is not not an  emotion that comes anywhere near the  sort of just a small sense of  satisfaction that I was witnessing the  law in action I was witnessing proper  civilized  International States from the Free World  behaving as they should so satisfaction  that no more  well Simon main it's been a real  privilege to talk to you today thanks  very much indeed for for joining us and  telling us a little bit about your son  Richard and your reaction to that  verdict we really appreciate it  thank you
 

